# We will calculate multiple population genetic metrics for the different species, such as nucleotide diversity (Pi),
# heterozygosity, Dxy, Fst (absolute and relative divergence). 
# For this, we need to extract sample names from the VCF file and calculate the different metrics.

####  Nucleotide diversity (Pi) ####
## To calculate PI, you can need a VCF file and a file including the sample IDs that are used in the VCF file.
## PI, aka the nucleotide diversity (π), is the average number of nucleotide differences per site between two sequences, within a population:
## the total pairwise differences at all sites / number of pairwise comparisons × number of sites

## To extract the IDs, we can use
bcftools query -l your_file.vcf.gz > samples.txt
## Then, we check the samples.txt and allocate them manually. The final tab-separated file should look something like, e.g.:
sample  population
ind1    spA
ind2    spA
ind3    spA
ind4    spB
ind5    spB
ind6    spB

## We will calculate PI using both for the whole-genome and sliding windows:
## We use sinteractive with the default settings for this:
## Whole genome, per species do
sinteractive
module load bio-apps
module load vcftools

## For Admixed1
vcftools \
  --gzvcf all_samples_DP8.AN10.376Inds_noCAXY.364inds.vcf.gz \
  --keep samples_Admi1.txt \
  --site-pi \
  --out Admi1_pi_sites
## Oneliner
# vcftools --gzvcf all_samples_DP8.AN10.376Inds_noCAXY.364inds.vcf.gz --keep samples_Admi1.txt --site-pi --out Admi1_pi_site

## For each species, we get PI values all sites in the genome. Using awk below, we calculate the mean over all sites.
## Note, change the "$3" if necessary, dpeneding where the PI values are in the "XY.sites.pi"-file
# Admi1
awk 'NR>1 {sum += $3; n++} END {if (n>0) print sum/n}' pop1_pi_sites.sites.pi
## NR>1 skips the header.
## Output: single number = mean π across all listed sites (including those with PI = 0, aka invariant sites).
## With this, we will receive one genomw-wide PI value for all hybrid or F. aquilonia samples
# 0.0521456

# F. aquilonia
vcftools --gzvcf all_samples_DP8.AN10.376Inds_noCAXY.364inds.vcf.gz --keep samples_aqui.txt --site-pi --out aqui_pi_site
awk 'NR>1 {sum += $3; n++} END {if (n>0) print sum/n}' aqui_pi_sites.sites.pi
# 0.0657245

